  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall begin not later than three years from the date of this decision.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended by Section 51 of the Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and specifications: [Location Plan, 0663 (00) 01, 0663 (00) 02 Existing Ground Floor Plan, 0663 (00) 02 Existing First Floor Plan, 0663 (00) 04, 0663 (00) 05, 0663 (00) 07, 0663 (00) 09, 0663 (01) 01, 0663 (01) 02 Proposed Ground Floor, 0663 (01) 01, 0663 (01) 04, 0663 (01) 05, 0663 (01) 07, 0663 (01) 09, Design, Access and Heritage Statement and Fire Safety Strategy Statement. Received: 04/03/2025\r\n0663 (00) 06 A, 0663 (00) 08 A, 0663 (01) 06 A and 0663 (01) 08 A. Received: 01/05/2025].\r\nReason: In order to ensure the development is carried out in accordance with the planning permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the development hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building, unless otherwise shown on the approved plans.\r\nReason: In order to safeguard the appearance of the area.",
    "Condition : 4 - The basement hereby permitted shall at no time be used or occupied as a separate dwelling independent of the main house and shall not be used as sleeping accommodation.\r\nReason: In order to ensure that adequate living standards are maintained and to protect neighbours' living conditions.\r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - The windows to be fitted on the roof face of the dwelling shall be black-framed and traditional, conservation-style.\r\nReason: In order to safeguard the architectural and historic interest of the conservation area."
